      {
        "target_formid": "0024A0AA",
        "record_type": "LSCR",
        "field": "DESC",
        "english": "Exiting back to the Main Menu will create an Exitsave. Next time you play and load the Exitsave, it will delete itself until the next time you exit back to the Main Menu."
      },
      {
        "target_formid": "00249F8C",
        "record_type": "LSCR",
        "field": "DESC",
        "english": "In Survival, both you and your companion's Carry Weight has been significantly reduced. Exceeding your carry weight reduces your Endurance and Agility stats, and periodically damages your legs and health. Think of your back!"
      },
      {
        "target_formid": "00249F8B",
        "record_type": "LSCR",
        "field": "DESC",
        "english": "In Survival, Stimpaks and Ammo both have weight. Bullets and shells have a small amount of weight, which varies by caliber. Heavier items such as fusion cores, rockets, and mini-nukes can really drag you down."
      },
      {
        "target_formid": "00249F8A",
        "record_type": "LSCR",
        "field": "DESC",
        "english": "In Survival, large doses of Caffeine, such as that found in Nuka-Cola Quantum, gives you a short reprieve from your tiredness, possibly buying you time to finish a fight or find a bed."
      },
      {
        "target_formid": "00249F89",
        "record_type": "LSCR",
        "field": "DESC",
        "english": "In Survival, a food's bonus effects, such as increased carry weight from Radstag steak, will only apply if eaten when you are not currently hungry. Make sure to take care of the basics before eating for bonuses."
      },
      {
        "target_formid": "00249F88",
        "record_type": "LSCR",
        "field": "DESC",
        "english": "In Survival, if your companion goes down during combat, you must heal them before they can get back up. If you leave the area without healing them, they will return home to recover."
      },
      {
        "target_formid": "00249F87",
        "record_type": "LSCR",
        "field": "DESC",
        "english": "In Survival, Crippled limbs will no longer auto-heal after combat. You will remain crippled until you are healed from a Stimpak or until you sleep it off."
      },
      {
        "target_formid": "00249F86",
        "record_type": "LSCR",
        "field": "DESC",
        "english": "In Survival, an items value is often a good way to determine how much hunger or thirst it might counter. Keep in mind, certain items may not give you the results you expect. For example, Chems and Alcohol dehydrate, Caffeine makes you hungry, etc."
      },
      {
        "target_formid": "00249F85",
        "record_type": "LSCR",
        "field": "DESC",
        "english": "In Survival, the type of bed you're sleeping in determines the length of time you're able to stay asleep. A sleeping bag will save your game and may save your life, but it'll never give you a full night's rest and the benefits that come with it."
      }
    ]
